28bo|n|A garment; clothing; especially, an upper or outer garment. ; An article of dress worn in token of grief; a mourning garment or badge; as, he wore a weed on his hat; especially, in the plural, mourning garb, as of a woman; as, a widow's weeds. ; A sudden illness or relapse, often attended with fever, which attacks women in childbed. ; Underbrush; low shrubs. ; Any plant growing in cultivated ground to the injury of the crop or desired vegetation, or to the disfigurement of the place; an unsightly, useless, or injurious plant. ; Fig.: Something unprofitable or troublesome; anything useless. ; An animal unfit to breed from. ; Tobacco, or a cigar.	a:12z6,93,5;mh9,83,2;e3m,29,4~12z6,93,5;e3m,29,4;mh9,83,2	v:1vkr,100,1;1vkz,93,4;1vkq,70,2~1vkz,93,4;1vkq,70,2;1vkr,100,1	n:1vkq,60,1~1vkq,60,1	N:mud,86,1;1t6k,73,2;zfz,64,3~zfz,64,3;1t6k,73,2;mud,86,1
